From 80953c33b3e08a0b599f0202155ab2608574f29f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 09:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] video-driver: vidc: shrink the COMV buffer at reconfig

msm_vidc_get_internal_buffers marks an internal buffer for reuse when
the size and count needed after a reconfig fit in the one already
held; release, destroy and create then skip it, and for the decoder's
COMV (collocated motion vector) buffer only HFI_PROP_COMV_BUFFER_COUNT
carries the new count. A reconfig that needs a smaller COMV, such as a
DRC to a lower resolution, keeps the larger buffer until the session
closes.

COMV normally grows at the first settings change, and with linear
capture the split-mode FIRST_IPSC branch reallocates there anyway,
which hid it.

Reallocate decoder COMV whenever its size changes. The old buffer is
released to the firmware and freed on its release done, as for a
larger one.

Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending [qualcomm-linux/video-driver]
---
 driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_driver.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_driver.c b/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_driver.c
index e3e579d5..8dc4dd4e 100644
--- a/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_driver.c
+++ b/driver/vidc/src/msm_vidc_driver.c
@@ -3447,7 +3447,9 @@ int msm_vidc_get_internal_buffers(struct msm_vidc_inst *inst,
 		buffers->size = buf_size;
 		buffers->min_count = buf_count;
 	} else if (buf_size && buf_size <= buffers->size &&
-		buf_count && buf_count <= buffers->min_count) {
+		buf_count && buf_count <= buffers->min_count &&
+		(buffer_type != MSM_VIDC_BUF_COMV || !is_decode_session(inst) ||
+		 buf_size == buffers->size)) {
 		buffers->reuse = true;
 	} else {
 		buffers->reuse = false;
